window.addEventListener("hashchange", route);</code></pre></div></div> <div class="paragraph" dir="auto">with history-based router.</div><ol start="2"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Replace all <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">href="#/${t.id}"</code> patterns and <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">href="#/"</code> with path-based. In template literals, <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">href="#/${t.id}"</code> appears in buildToolUI related cards and cardHTML. Change to <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">href="/${t.id}"</code>. Links <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">href="#/"</code> → <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">href="/"</code>. goSection calls on nav — replace nav links with direct hrefs to pages and keep Popular/PDF/Image section anchors using goSection with path "/". Update goSection to use history nav then scroll.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">In initTool crumb: <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">&lt;a href="#/"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;</code> → <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">&lt;a href="/"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;</code>.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Remove privacy/about/contact sections from renderHome, and add new page renderers renderPrivacy, renderAbout, renderContact with full content, titles, meta. Contact gets email card with mailto.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Add hash redirect snippet before route(): if hash route present, history.replaceState to path.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Update footer Company links to /privacy /about /contact /faq (faq keep section #faq? FAQ is on home; keep goSection for faq or link "/#faq"? With BrowserRouter, "/#faq" sets hash — popstate won't fire; but on load route() runs then browser scrolls to anchor? For hash on load, browser auto-scrolls after load. Simpler: keep FAQ as section link via goSection when on home. I'll make footer FAQ link goSection to 'faq' like before.)</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Also update burger menu: add About/Contact/Privacy links.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Also og:url/canonical in head point to pinkfile.tools — fine, they own... actually they haven't bought a domain yet; canonical pinkfile.tools may be aspirational. Leave it; maybe update on route.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Also update the header nav links.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me also handle scroll restoration: after pushState render, scrollTo top.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">popstate listener re-renders.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Implement navigate(path) helper:</div><div data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-bfaabce6="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-bfaabce6="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-bfaabce6="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-bfaabce6="" class="segment-code-lang">plain</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-bfaabce6=""><div data-v-ab0641ea="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-ab0641ea="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h25