ta-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">#</code> then <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">\/</code>. My string: <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">replace(/^#\\//, "")</code> → renders <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">replace(/^#\//, "")</code>. Should match...</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Oh wait — the issue: in THIS cell, the pages_js replacement already inserted text containing <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">/* ================= Router (clean URLs, no #) ================= */</code>, fine. But maybe the mismatch is in <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">location.hash !== "#/"</code> line? Original: <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">if (location.hash !== "#/" &amp;&amp; location.hash !== ""){ location.hash = "#/"; ...</code> — matches my literal.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Hmm, but actually — the previous cell (step 1-2) ran and modified <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">src</code>, but variables persist across executions... The error trace shows it's In[4]. Steps 1-2 in In[3] modified src. Then In[4] step 3: <code data-v-bfaabce6="" data-v-048cb31c="" class="segment-code-inline">src = src.replace('/* ================= Router ================= */', pages_js)</code> succeeded. So why old_router not in src?</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Ah — I see it! In the original HTML file, the router block line is:
